# kills: DI: the sheet serves DING, TOP RIM NOTES, TOP INNER (CYCLOPS/MUTANT) NOTE and BOTTOM NOTES in that order before #scale-box, each a text input with autocapitalize off, enterkeyhint next and BOTTOM done
# suite: node --test --test-name-pattern ^DI:.the.sheet.serves.DING tests/app.test.js
# The scale line goes back above the four note fields.
diff --git a/index.html b/index.html
--- a/index.html
+++ b/index.html
@@ -1594,6 +1594,32 @@ html.about-open{overflow:hidden}
          parseSeed); focusing one dims the other. One variable, inputPath, says
          which is active. The live region is the last child so the order the
          SG: N-A2 tests pin is untouched. -->
+    <div class="fieldrow">
+      <label class="sheetlabel" for="scale-box">SCALE: (DING) TOP NOTES | OPTIONAL INNER NOTES</label>
+      <span class="sheetlabel" id="scale-label-2">[NOTE] = A BOTTOM NOTE</span>
+      <div id="scale-box-wrap" data-grow="[C3] [D3] (E3) [F#3] [G3] [A3] B3 [C4] D4 E4 F#4 G4 A4 B4 [C5] D5 E5 | F#5 G5 A5">
+        <textarea id="scale-box" rows="1" wrap="soft" autocapitalize="off" autocorrect="off"
+                  autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" enterkeyhint="go"
+                  aria-describedby="scale-label-2"
+                  placeholder="[C3] [D3] (E3) [F#3] [G3] [A3] B3 [C4] D4 E4 F#4 G4 A4 B4 [C5] D5 E5 | F#5 G5 A5"></textarea>
+      </div>
+      <div id="scale-parse"></div>
+      <!-- Owner feedback, 2026-09-21: a refusal rendered below the pan is
+           below the fold on an iPhone 14 with the keyboard up, so the user
+           retypes a seed whose reason they never saw. It belongs directly
+           under the field it is about, inside the same .fieldrow group.
+           This element carries SEED REFUSALS ONLY - it is not the sheet's
+           message area. #scale-msg keeps that job, in #scale-guidance below the scroll, because a
+           warning or a success notice is not about the field and must not
+           compete for this row. Refusals never go through say(): sharing one
+           reserved line with the parse line only works while exactly one of
+           the two is filled, and showRefusal()/showParse() are what make that
+           true rather than hoping every caller happens to agree. It carries
+           its own aria-live because #scale-sheet is aria-modal, which puts
+           the page-level .announce outside the dialog and out of reach. -->
+      <div id="scale-refusal" aria-live="polite"></div>
+      <p class="sheethint" id="scale-line-note"></p>
+    </div>
     <div id="scale-fields" role="group" aria-labelledby="scale-fields-head">
